## Why This Is Asked

This angle tests cross-account SAP design with per-BU isolation, JIT operator access, and PrivateLink auditing.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-account IAM roles and SCPs
- AWS SSO with Just-In-Time elevation
- PrivateLink for SAP components
- Centralized auditing with CloudTrail/Config
- IaC patterns (CDK/CloudFormation)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal AWS CDK snippet creating cross-account trust role and a VPC endpoint service
import * as iam from 'aws-cdk-lib/aws-iam';
import * as ec2 from 'aws-cdk-lib/aws-ec2';
import { Stack, Construct } from 'aws-cdk-lib';
export class SapCrossAccountStack extends Stack {
  constructor(scope: Construct, id: string) {
    super(scope, id);
    const crossAccountRole = new iam.Role(this, 'SapCrossAccountRole', {
      assumedBy: new iam.AccountPrincipal('111122223333'),
      description: 'Cross-account trust role for SAP BU access',
      roleName: 'SapCrossAccountRole',
    });
    crossAccountRole.addToPolicy(new iam.PolicyStatement({
      actions: ['s3:ListBucket','s3:GetObject'],
      resources: ['arn:aws:s3:::sap-artifacts-*','arn:aws:s3:::sap-artifacts-*/*']
    }));
    new ec2.CfnVPCEndpointService(this, 'SapVpceService', {
      serviceName: 'com.amazonaws.vpce.sap',
      acceptanceRequired: false
    });
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate JIT elevation and audit trails across accounts?
- What tagging/monitoring strategy ensures cost and compliance visibility?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a cross-account, auditable backup strategy for SAP HANA on EC2 that enforces immutability and cross-account access control.

## Key Concepts

- Immutable backups with S3 Object Lock (COMPLIANCE)
- Cross-account IAM roles and trust policies
- KMS CMK grants for cross-account encryption/decryption
- AWS Backup vault policies and cross-account access
- S3 bucket versioning and access policies

## Code Example

```hcl
# Terraform snippet: immutable SAP backups with cross-account access
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "sap_backups" {
  bucket = "sap-backups-prod"
  acl    = "private"

  versioning {
    enabled = true
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_object_lock_configuration" "lock" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.sap_backups.id
  object_lock_enabled = true

  rule {
    default_retention {
      mode = "COMPLIANCE"
      days = 3650
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "sap_backup_cross_account_role" {
  name = "sap-backup-cross-account-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow",
      Principal = {
        AWS = "arn:aws:iam::BACKUP_ACCOUNT_ID:root"
      },
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
    }]
  })
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you rotate the CMK without service disruption?
- How would you validate backups remain immutable after policy changes?
